# Separate branches for ATH and Assistants

Unless the user explicitly says to combine them, ATH and Assistants changes go on different branches, each started from `main`.

- An ATH branch may change `PetelATH/**` and ATH docs (`docs/agents/apps/petel-ath.md`, `docs/agents/apps/petel-ath-reports-excel.md`).
- An Assistants branch may change `PetelAssistants/**` and Assistants docs (`docs/agents/apps/petel-assistants.md`, `docs/agents/apps/petel-assistants-domain.md`).
- Do not add the other app's files to the current branch. If a task needs both apps, stop and split it into two branches.
- `shared/` and cross-app infra (`infra/`, `docs/aws-setup.md`, `docs/azure-setup.md`) stay on the branch of the app task that needs them. A shared change both apps must take together waits until the user says to combine it.

Examples:

- School-year wizard → branch from `main`, touch only `PetelATH/**`.
- Salary month summary → branch from `main`, touch only `PetelAssistants/**`.
- User says "do both on this branch" → one branch is allowed.
